hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16523","He said: Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Asim, meaning Ibn Ubaydullah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said in the Farewell Hajj: Your slaves, your slaves, your slaves, feed them from what you eat and clothe them from what you wear, and if they commit a sin you do not wish to forgive, then sell the servants of Allah and do not punish them."
